{"id":"mahabharata-1-109","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":109,"title":"नवाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 109 · Pandu kills the sage Kindama","summary":{"en":"Hunting in the forest, Pandu shoots a buck mating with its doe. The deer is the sage Kindama in disguise, who, dying, curses Pandu to die himself if he ever approaches a woman in love.","kn":"ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಬೇಟೆಯಾಡುವಾಗ ಪಾಂಡು ಹೆಣ್ಣಿನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕೂಡಿದ್ದ ಗಂಡುಜಿಂಕೆಗೆ ಬಾಣ ಹೊಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆ ಜಿಂಕೆ ವೇಷಧಾರಿ ಕಿಂದಮ ಋಷಿ; ಸಾಯುತ್ತಾ ಅವನು ಪಾಂಡು ಎಂದಾದರೂ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇಮದಿಂದ ಸೇರಿದರೆ ಸಾಯುವನೆಂದು ಶಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वन में शिकार करते हुए पाण्डु मृगी के साथ संगम करते एक मृग को बाण मारते हैं। वह मृग वेशधारी ऋषि किन्दम है, जो मरते हुए शाप देता है कि पाण्डु यदि कभी प्रेम से स्त्री के पास जाएँगे तो मर जाएँगे।","te":"అడవిలో వేటాడుతుండగా పాండురాజు ఆడజింకతో కూడిన మగజింకపై బాణం వేస్తాడు. ఆ జింక మారువేషంలోని కిందమ ఋషి; చనిపోతూ పాండురాజు ఎన్నడైనా ప్రేమతో స్త్రీని సమీపిస్తే మరణిస్తాడని శపిస్తాడు.","ta":"காட்டில் வேட்டையாடும்போது பாண்டு பெண்மானுடன் கூடியிருந்த ஆண்மான் மீது அம்பெய்கிறான். அந்த மான் மாறுவேடத்திலிருந்த கிந்தம முனிவர்; இறக்கும்போது அவர், பாண்டு எப்போதாவது காதலுடன் பெண்ணை அணுகினால் இறப்பான் என்று சபிக்கிறார்.","ml":"കാട്ടിൽ വേട്ടയാടുന്ന പാണ്ഡു, ഇണചേരുന്ന ഒരു മാനിനെ വെടിവെക്കുന്നു. ആ മാൻ വേഷം മാറിയ കിന്ദമൻ ഋഷിയാണ്; മരണത്തോടടുക്കുമ്പോൾ, സ്നേഹത്തോടെ ഒരു സ്ത്രീയെ സമീപിച്ചാൽ പാണ്ഡു മരിക്കട്ടെ എന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ശപിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.109; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"संभवपर्व","titleEn":"Sambhava Parva (Origins)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथितो धार्तराष्ट्राणामार्षः संभव उत्तमः ।\nअमानुषो मानुषाणां भवता ब्रह्मवित्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have told me, best of the knowers of Brahman, of the excellent and sage-like births of the sons of Dhritarashtra, which were beyond human among men."}},{"n":2,"text":"नामधेयानि चाप्येषां कथ्यमानानि भागशः ।\nत्वत्तः श्रुतानि मे ब्रह्मन्पाण्डवानां तु कीर्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their names too, told one by one, I have heard from you, brahmin. Now tell me of the Pandavas."}},{"n":3,"text":"ते हि सर्वे महात्मानो देवराजपराक्रमाः ।\nत्वयैवांशावतरणे देवभागाः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those great souls, all equal in valor to the king of the gods, were declared by you yourself to be portions of the gods, in the account of the descent of the divine portions."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्मादिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुमतिमानुषकर्मणाम् ।\nतेषामाजननं सर्वं वैशंपायन कीर्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I wish to hear about the superhuman deeds of those men; Vaishampayana, tell me the whole account of their births."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"राजा पाण्डुर्महारण्ये मृगव्यालनिषेविते ।\nवने मैथुनकालस्थं ददर्श मृगयूथपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Pandu, in a great forest frequented by deer and beasts of prey, saw a leader of a herd of deer at the time of mating."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततस्तां च मृगीं तं च रुक्मपुङ्खैः सुपत्रिभिः ।\nनिर्बिभेद शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः पाण्डुः पञ्चभिराशुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Pandu pierced both the doe and the stag with five swift, sharp, well-feathered, gold-fletched arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"स च राजन्महातेजा ऋषिपुत्रस्तपोधनः ।\nभार्यया सह तेजस्वी मृगरूपेण संगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That stag, O king, was a sage's son of great radiance and wealth of austerity, who was united with his wife in the form of a deer."}},{"n":8,"text":"संसक्तस्तु तया मृग्या मानुषीमीरयन्गिरम् ।\nक्षणेन पतितो भूमौ विललापाकुलेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entangled with the doe, he spoke in human speech, fell to the ground in an instant, and cried out, his senses confused."}},{"text":"मृग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The deer said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"काममन्युपरीतापि बुद्ध्यङ्गरहितापि च ।\nवर्जयन्ति नृशंसानि पापेष्वभिरता नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even men given to sin, though seized by desire and anger and devoid of understanding, avoid such cruel acts."}},{"n":10,"text":"न विधिं ग्रसते प्रज्ञा प्रज्ञां तु ग्रसते विधिः ।\nविधिपर्यागतानर्थान्प्रज्ञा न प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wisdom does not swallow fate; fate swallows wisdom. Wisdom cannot grasp what fate brings about."}},{"n":11,"text":"शश्वद्धर्मात्मनां मुख्ये कुले जातस्य भारत ।\nकामलोभाभिभूतस्य कथं ते चलिता मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You were born, Bharata, in a family always foremost in righteous souls; how has your mind swerved, overcome by desire and greed?\""}},{"text":"पाण्डुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Pandu said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"शत्रूणां या वधे वृत्तिः सा मृगाणां वधे स्मृता ।\nराज्ञां मृग न मां मोहात्त्वं गर्हयितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The rule for killing enemies is held to apply to killing deer; deer, you should not blame me from confusion, for I am a king."}},{"n":13,"text":"अच्छद्मनामायया च मृगाणां वध इष्यते ।\nस एव धर्मो राज्ञां तु तद्विद्वान्किं नु गर्हसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The killing of deer, by fair means or by a trick, is permitted; this is the king's dharma, so why do you blame me, knowing this?"}},{"n":14,"text":"अगस्त्यः सत्रमासीनश्चचार मृगयामृषिः ।\nआरण्यान्सर्वदैवत्यान्मृगान्प्रोक्ष्य महावने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage Agastya, engaged in a sacrifice, hunted, and, having consecrated all the forest deer to the gods, offered them in the great forest."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रमाणदृष्टधर्मेण कथमस्मान्विगर्हसे ।\nअगस्त्यस्याभिचारेण युष्माकं वै वपा हुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that dharma, seen by authority, how can you blame us? By Agastya's rite, your fat was offered in sacrifice.\""}},{"text":"मृग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The deer said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"न रिपून्वै समुद्दिश्य विमुञ्चन्ति पुरा शरान् ।\nरन्ध्र एषां विशेषेण वधकालः प्रशस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"People do not loose arrows on enemies first without warning; when one is at a disadvantage, that is held to be the best time to kill.\""}},{"text":"पाण्डुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Pandu said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रमत्तमप्रमत्तं वा विवृतं घ्नन्ति चौजसा ।\nउपायैरिषुभिस्तीक्ष्णैः कस्मान्मृग विगर्हसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They kill by force an enemy who is careless, or careful, or exposed, by means of tricks and sharp arrows; why do you blame me, deer?\""}},{"text":"मृग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The deer said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"नाहं घ्नन्तं मृगान्राजन्विगर्हे आत्मकारणात् ।\nमैथुनं तु प्रतीक्ष्यं मे स्यात्त्वयेहानृशंसतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I do not blame you for killing deer, king, on your own account; but you should have waited, out of mercy, until I finished my mating."}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वभूतहिते काले सर्वभूतेप्सिते तथा ।\nको हि विद्वान्मृगं हन्याच्चरन्तं मैथुनं वने ।\nपुरुषार्थफलं कान्तं यत्त्वया वितथं कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a season good for all beings and desired by all beings, what wise man would kill a deer roaming in the forest while it mates? You have spoiled that lovely fruit of man's aim."}},{"n":20,"text":"पौरवाणामृषीणां च तेषामक्लिष्टकर्मणाम् ।\nवंशे जातस्य कौरव्य नानुरूपमिदं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You were born in the line of the Pauravas and of those sages of unwearied deeds, Kuru's descendant; this does not suit you."}},{"n":21,"text":"नृशंसं कर्म सुमहत्सर्वलोकविगर्हितम् ।\nअस्वर्ग्यमयशस्यं च अधर्मिष्ठं च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"This act is cruel, very great, condemned by all the world, bars heaven, brings no fame, and is most unrighteous, Bharata."}},{"n":22,"text":"स्त्रीभोगानां विशेषज्ञः शास्त्रधर्मार्थतत्त्ववित् ।\nनार्हस्त्वं सुरसंकाश कर्तुमस्वर्ग्यमीदृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know the special features of the enjoyments of women and the truth about dharma and the scriptures; shining like a god, you should not do such a thing as bars heaven."}},{"n":23,"text":"त्वया नृशंसकर्तारः पापाचाराश्च मानवाः ।\nनिग्राह्याः पार्थिवश्रेष्ठ त्रिवर्गपरिवर्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By you, best of kings, men who do cruel and sinful acts and give up the three aims of life should be restrained."}},{"n":24,"text":"किं कृतं ते नरश्रेष्ठ निघ्नतो मामनागसम् ।\nमुनिं मूलफलाहारं मृगवेषधरं नृप ।\nवसमानमरण्येषु नित्यं शमपरायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What have you gained, best of men, by killing me, who had done no wrong, a sage who lives on roots and fruit, in the form of a deer, who always lives in the forests devoted to peace?"}},{"n":25,"text":"त्वयाहं हिंसितो यस्मात्तस्मात्त्वामप्यसंशयम् ।\nद्वयोर्नृशंसकर्तारमवशं काममोहितम् ।\nजीवितान्तकरो भाव एवमेवागमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since I have been killed by you, without doubt the same state that ends life will come to you too, who did a cruel deed against two helpless ones, deluded by desire."}},{"n":26,"text":"अहं हि किंदमो नाम तपसाप्रतिमो मुनिः ।\nव्यपत्रपन्मनुष्याणां मृग्यां मैथुनमाचरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am a sage named Kindama, unequaled in austerity; out of shame before men I was mating with a doe."}},{"n":27,"text":"मृगो भूत्वा मृगैः सार्धं चरामि गहने वने ।\nन तु ते ब्रह्महत्येयं भविष्यत्यविजानतः ।\nमृगरूपधरं हत्वा मामेवं काममोहितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having become a deer, I roam in the dense forest with the deer. Yet this will not be the sin of killing a brahmin for you, since you did not know, though you killed me in deer form, so overcome by desire."}},{"n":28,"text":"अस्य तु त्वं फलं मूढ प्राप्स्यसीदृशमेव हि ।\nप्रियया सह संवासं प्राप्य कामविमोहितः ।\nत्वमप्यस्यामवस्थायां प्रेतलोकं गमिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, fool, you will get just such a fruit for this: when you are with your beloved, confused by desire, in that very state you will go to the world of the dead."}},{"n":29,"text":"अन्तकाले च संवासं यया गन्तासि कान्तया ।\nप्रेतराजवशं प्राप्तं सर्वभूतदुरत्ययम् ।\nभक्त्या मतिमतां श्रेष्ठ सैव त्वामनुयास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the time of death, the very beloved with whom you are united will follow you in devotion, best of the wise, when you are under the power of the king of the dead, whom all beings find hard to cross."}},{"n":30,"text":"वर्तमानः सुखे दुःखं यथाहं प्रापितस्त्वया ।\nतथा सुखं त्वां संप्राप्तं दुःखमभ्यागमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you have brought me suffering while I was in happiness, so suffering will come to you when you are in happiness.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा सुदुःखार्तो जीवितात्स व्ययुज्यत ।\nमृगः पाण्डुश्च शोकार्तः क्षणेन समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, in very great pain, he gave up his life; and Pandu, grieving over the deer, was in an instant overcome by sorrow."}}]}]}